THE ARMS  (each is the previous one plus the named change)
----------------------------------------------------------
base        6c17d8c, unmodified
slotflag    per-slot live-flag bytes: publish and release become plain stores,
            the two locked RMWs (fetch_or / fetch_and) are gone
leaf        + `add`'s fast path made a frameless leaf (try_lock with a cold
            outlined contended path; overlap_panic takes 7 scalars instead of a
            25-byte tuple). 0x80 frame + 3 stp/ldp pairs gone, 143 -> 117 insns
chain/final + `mask == 0` instances skip the shift load, both block divisions
            and the multiplicative hash entirely
lm          + `live_mask` straight-line when `allocated <= 1` (one load, no
            `rbit`/`clz`, no loop) — the measured steady state
alloc0      + `alloc` straight-line when the shard is empty (slot 0, constant
            store offsets) and `allocated` written once instead of twice
v2 SHIPPED  + `live_mask` drops its `allocated == 0` sub-branch, and the empty
            -shard `alloc` stores `mutable` whole instead of read-modify-write
fold        REVERTED. one-shard body duplicated so shard 0's address folds
findeo      REVERTED. `find` early-out on `occupied == 0`
chain3      REVERTED. findeo + dropping the pre-lock `state` check
addnop      THROWAWAY `probe-addnop`: keeps the call, deletes the body
untracked   THROWAWAY `probe-untracked`: no tracker at all (the ceiling)


